NS\t19\nSection 1. Limitations on Activities\t19\nSection 2. Prohibition Against Private Inurement\t19\nSection 3. Distribution of Assets\t19\nARTICLE XV AMENDMENTS\t19\nSection 1. Proposal Submission Requirements\t19\nSection 2. Review Process\t20\nSection 3. Ratification Criteria\t20\nSection 4. Ratification Process\t20\nSection 5. Emergency Amendments\t20\nSection 6. Notification and Record-Keeping\t21\nSection 7. Periodic Review\t21\nARTICLE XVI CONSTRUCTION AND TERMS\t21\n\nNAME AND PURPOSE\nName\nThe name of the organization shall be the Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0 (“RIIS 2.0”). RIIS 2.0 shall be a nonprofit organization incorporated under the laws of the State of California and organized under California’s Nonprofit Public Benefit Corporation Law (CA Corp. Code § 5110 et seq.) (“CNCL”).\nIRC Section 501(c)(3) Purposes\nRIIS 2.0 is organized exclusively for charitable, scholarly, scientific, and educational purposes. The specific objectives and purposes are to be a venue for our researchers in their execution and dissemination of their scholarly research in the public interest. RIIS 2.0 provides scholarly researchers with membership  affiliation, community, and dissemination opportunities. RIIS 2.0 does not itself conduct, sponsor, or direct research as an institution. The Council may in the future choose to expand the institute’s activities or mandate through revisions to these bylaws and associated policies.\nRIIS 2.0 offers an inclusive academic community of belonging to scholars committed to truth and empathy to share ideas and grow intellectually, to improve and develop their capabilities, and to help scholars establish new contacts and collaborations. \nRIIS 2.0 is a platform outside of traditional academia that invites scholars from around the world with unique perspectives to share their voices and address issues in their purview, fostering opportunities for unique academic insights. Scholars with a broad range of experiences can 