nding of our world. Scholars pursue their research in the way that works best for them. We expect that Scholars will be honest and thoughtful, both in scholarship and in their interactions with the community and world at large.\nEmpathy demands that one act in good faith and assume good faith from others. RIIS 2.0 expects Scholars to interact in a spirit of kindness, generosity, and patience. We are a highly interdisciplinary and international community with Fellows who may have very different perspectives and backgrounds.\nNondiscrimination\nRIIS 2.0 and its officers, Councilors, employees, and persons served by RIIS 2.0 shall be selected in a non-discriminatory manner with respect to race, color, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or social origin, property, birth or other status such as disability, age, marital and family status, sexual orientation and gender identity, health status, place of residence, and economic and social situation in accordance with local, state and federal law.\nBelonging\nRIIS 2.0 and its Scholars, staff, and Council are also committed to incorporating the values of our Belonging Policy in the governance and operations of this Institute. RIIS 2.0 believes everyone has the right to work in a professional environment where their knowledge, skills, and abilities are the factors for their success. RIIS 2.0 expects all affiliated with the organization to maintain standards of propriety, treat everyone professionally, and act without bias. RIIS 2.0 has a zero-tolerance policy for sexual harassment. These values shall be adopted by the Fellows and Associates and be codified in a Belonging Policy adopted by the Council.\nRIIS 2.0 acknowledges the values expressed in the Belonging Policy as foundational principles of the Institute. RIIS 2.0 seeks to expand the academic landscape by providing a heterogeneous body of scholars with equitable access to opportunities, resources, and support.\nFELLOWSHIP\nDefinition\nA Fellow must fulfill membership requirements as outlined below and in the policies and procedures documentation adopted from time to time by the governing body of RIIS 2.0 (such body, the “Council”, and such documentation, the “Policies and Procedures”). \nEligibility for Fellowship\nTo be considered for membership, an applicant must demonstrate academic achievement and scholarly commitment, the determination of which shall be at the recommendation of the Affiliation Working Group and, ultimately, the approval of the Council. Applications for affiliation shall be open to any scholar in pursuit of academic scholarship. All Fellows agree to follow the code of conduct and ethics. Fellowship is granted after the completion and receipt of a membership application, payment of annual dues, and recommendation to the Council by the Affiliation Working Group. The Council shall oversee the membership enrollment process.\nAnnual Dues\nFellowship requires the payment of annual dues. Continued membership is contingent upon being up-to-date on membership dues. Procedures for determining dues will be defined within the Policies and Procedures, with any changes approved by a vote of the membership. A copy of the current dues will be available on the website.\nRights of Fellows\nFellowship shall entitle Fellows to (i) participate in the programs of RIIS 2.0; (ii) have the right to vote on the election or removal of Councilors, on the disposition of all or substantially all of the assets of the corporation, on any merger and its principal terms and any amendment of those terms, and on any election to dissolve the corporation, and to participate in any votes put to the membership by the Council; and (iii) to request RIIS 2.0 to administer the Fellow’s awards, grants and contracts.\n"},{"ty":"as","st":"list","si":4391,"ei":4391,"sm":{"ls_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":true,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_lsp_i":false,"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr