 of all officers, agents, and employees of RIIS 2.0;\nSupervise all officers, agents, and employees of the corporation to ensure that their duties are performed properly;\nMeet at such times and places as required by these Bylaws or by resolution of the Council.\nRegister their email addresses with the Secretary, and notices of meetings emailed to them at such email addresses shall be valid notices thereof.\nOfficer Roles and Duties\nThere shall be at least three Officers on the Council, consisting of a Chair, Secretary, and Treasurer. The Past Chair shall assist the current principal officers, as needed. Other Officers may be appointed by the Council as needed.\nOfficers, other than the Past Chair, are selected from among current Councilors by the Council every year and serve 1-year terms in their role, but may be re-appointed by the Council. There is a 3-year term limit to serve as Chair. A past Chair may serve another term as Chair after three (3) years of not serving as Chair. No Councilor may hold more than one Officer role at a time, except as a temporary necessity for up to 6 months.\nChair\nThe Chair shall be responsible for convening regularly scheduled Council meetings and shall preside or arrange for another Councilor to preside at each meeting of the Council and at all meetings of the Fellows.\nThe Chair shall be the chief executive officer of the corporation in the event that the position is vacant. The Chair shall perform all duties as may be required by law, by the Articles of Incorporation, or by these Bylaws, or which may be prescribed from time to time by the Council.\nSecretary\nThe Secretary shall perform all duties as may be required by law, by the Articles of Incorporation, other relevant sections of these Bylaws, as well as relevant Policies and Procedures, or which may be assigned to them from time to time by the Council. The Secretary shall be responsible for Council meeting agendas and notes, for the archiving of these and other legal documents, and for managing the seal of the organization.\nTreasurer\nThe Treasurer shall perform all duties as may be required by law, by the Articles of Incorporation, or by these Bylaws, or which may be prescribed from time to time by the Council in accordance with the Policies and Procedures. The Treasurer shall be the bookkeeper for the corporation in the event that professional staff are not hired for that role.\nPast Chair\nPast Chairs shall serve as ex officio, non-voting members of the Council for one year following the conclusion of their most recent term as Chair, provided they are not continuing as a voting Council member. If a Chair is re-elected to the Council, this ex officio status shall not take effect until they no longer serve as a voting Council member.\nVacancies\nIn the event of a vacancy on the Council, remaining Councilors may appoint interim Councilors to serve for the remainder of the full term of the Councilor for which the vacancy was created or occurred and until such Councilor’s successor shall have been elected and qualified; provided, however, that in the event of a vacancy resulting in fewer Councilors than the minimum of three (3) required by CNCL, the following procedures should be followed:\nTemporary Suspension of Certain Decisions: No major decisions (such as bylaw amendments or financial commitments) may be made until the minimum number of Councilors is restored.\nEmergency Appointment Process: In the event of a vacancy resulting in fewer than the minimum number of Councilors, remaining Council members may appoint interim Councilors until an election by Fellows can be conducted.\nElection by Fellows: The Secretary must receive nominations for new officers. These nominations shall be voted upon at the next Annual Meeting if it occurs in less than four months, or at a Special Meeting to be called for the election within four months, whichever is earlier.\n"},{"ty":"as","st":"list","si":17239,"ei":17239,"sm":{"ls_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts