ript><script nonce="73eq18GWYhoYAuJk-FdczQ">DOCS_modelChunkParseStart = new Date().getTime();</script><script nonce="73eq18GWYhoYAuJk-FdczQ">DOCS_modelChunk = {"chunk":[{"ty":"is","ibi":21449,"s":"If there is a vacancy for an Officer position, the Council shall appoint a qualified Councilor to fill the Officer position as soon as feasible.\nResignation \u0026 Removal\nResignation from the Council must be in writing and received by the Secretary. \nRemoval by Fellows\u000b\u000b\tFellows entitled to vote may remove any Councilor, with or without cause, by approval of a majority of all Fellows entitled to vote, subject to any cumulative voting protections provided under California Corporations Code §5222(b).\nRemoval by the Council for Cause\u000b\u000bThe Council may remove any Councilor for cause by approval of a majority of the Councilors then in office, provided that a quorum is present, for any of the following reasons as defined in California Corporations Code §5222(a):\u000b\u000ba. The Councilor has been declared of unsound mind by a final order of the court.\u000b\u000bb. The Councilor has been convicted of a felony.\u000b\u000bc. The Councilor has been found by a final order or judgment to have breached fiduciary duties to the Institute under California Corporations Code §5231.\u000b\u000bd. The Councilor has failed to meet attendance requirements, as defined in these Bylaws or Policies, after written notice and opportunity to respond.\nRemoval of Appointed Councilors\u000b\u000bA Councilor appointed by the Council to fill a vacancy may be removed at any time by approval of a majority of the Councilors then in office, unless the appointment was made by the Fellows or another body with the exclusive right of appointment.\nProcedure for Removal\u000b\u000b1. Notice of the proposed removal must be given at least ten (10) days in advance of the meeting at which the removal will be considered, and must state the grounds for removal.\u000b\u000b2. The Councilor subject to removal shall have the opportunity to be heard before a final vote is taken.\u000b\u000b3. Removal becomes effective immediately upon approval unless otherwise stated in the motion for removal.\nEffect of Removal and Vacancies\nA removed Councilor’s position shall be deemed vacant as of the effective date of removal. The vacancy shall be filled in accordance with the vacancy-filling procedures in these Bylaws.\u000b\u000bRemoval shall not invalidate any prior action taken by the Council prior to the effective date of removal.\nCompensation\nCouncilors are volunteers and may not be compensated for their services as Councilors, but may be reimbursed for their reasonable out-of-pocket expenses incurred in connection with the performance of their duties as Councilors. Councilors may be compensated for their personal and professional services rendered to or on behalf of the RIIS 2.0 if approved in advance by the Council and subject to compliance with RIIS 2.0’s Policies and Procedures.\nIndemnification by the corporation of Councilors\nThe Councilors and officers of RIIS 2.0 shall be indemnified by RIIS 2.0 to the fullest extent permissible under the laws of California.\nInsurance for corporate agents\nExcept as may be otherwise provided under provisions of law, the Council may adopt a resolution authorizing the purchase and maintenance of insurance on behalf of any agent of the corporation (including a director, officer, employee, or other agent of the corporation) against liabilities asserted against or incurred by the agent in such capacity or arising out of the agent’s status as such, whether or not the corporation would have the power to indemnify the agent against such liability under the Articles of Incorporation, these Bylaws, or provisions of law.\nMEETINGS OF THE COUNCIL\nRegular Meetings\nThe Council shall meet at least quarterly.\nSpecial Meetings\nSpecial meetings may be called by the Chair or a simple majority of Councilors.\nQuorum\nA quorum of Council shall consist of at least two-thirds of the number of Councilors currently authorized by the Council pursuant to these Bylaws. Except as otherwise provided under the Articles of Incorporation, these Bylaws, or provisions of law, no business shall be considered by the Council at any meeting at which the required quorum is not present, and the only motion which the Chair shall entertain at such meeting is a motion to adjourn; provided, however, that a meeting at which a quorum is initially present may continue to transact business, notwithstanding the withdrawal of councilors from the meeting, if any action taken is approved by at least a majority of the required quorum for that meeting pursuant to the provisions of Section 4 below.\n"},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":21593,"ei":21593,"sm":{"ps_awao_i":false,"ps_ifl":36.0,"ps_ls":1.0,"ps_sa_i":false,"ps_lslm_i":true,"ps_sm_i":true,"ps_ifl_i":false,"ps_ls_i":false,"ps_sa":12.0,"ps_awao":true}},{"ty":"as","st":"list","si":21615,"ei":21615,"sm":{"ls_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":true,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_lsp_i":false,"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_lsp":{"lspp_points":0.0,"lsp_type":0},"ts_tw":400},"ls_id":"kix.list.1","ls_nest":1}},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":21615,"ei":21615,"sm":{"ps_klt_i":true,"ps_awao_i":true,"ps_sm_i":false,"ps_ls_i":true,"ps_ir_i":true,"ps_bl_i":true,"ps_sd_i":true,"ps_hdid":"h.szxma7212i1b","ps_sb_i":true,"ps_ifl":36.0,"ps_sa_i":true,"ps_lslm_i":true,"ps_br_i":true,"ps_sm":1,"ps_bbtw_i":true,"ps_hd":2,"ps_kwn_i":true,"ps_bt_i":true,"ps_ifl_i":false,"ps_bb_i":true,"ps_pbb_i":true}},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":21695,"ei":21695,"sm":{"ps_awao_i":false,"ps_ifl":36.0,"ps_ls":1.0,"ps_sa_i":false,"ps_lslm_i"